{"tool_name":"deepimagej","contents":["neubias","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"DeepImageJ","home":"https://deepimagej.github.io/deepimagej/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A user-friendly plugin to run deep learning models in ImageJ. Websites for you and your projects, hosted directly from your GitHub repository. Just edit, push, and your changes are live.\n\nDeepImageJ is a user-friendly plugin that enables the use of a variety of pre-trained deep learning models in ImageJ and Fiji. The plugin bridges the gap between deep learning and standard life-science applications. DeepImageJ runs image-to-image operations on a standard CPU-based computer and does not require any deep learning expertise.","addition_date":"2020-01-09T17:54:30Z","last_update_date":"2020-12-20T10:44:02Z","tool_type":["Plug-in"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:DeepImageJ","edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Deisotoping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3629"},{"term":"Editing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3096"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]}],"name":"DeepImageJ","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/799270"}],"topic":[{"term":"Bioengineering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3398"},{"term":"Imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382"},{"term":"Informatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0605"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"DeepImageJ","home":"https://bio.tools/DeepImageJ","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A user-friendly plugin to run deep learning models in ImageJ. Websites for you and your projects, hosted directly from your GitHub repository. Just edit, push, and your changes are live.\n\nDeepImageJ is a user-friendly plugin that enables the use of a variety of pre-trained deep learning models in ImageJ and Fiji. The plugin bridges the gap between deep learning and standard life-science applications. DeepImageJ runs image-to-image operations on a standard CPU-based computer and does not require any deep learning expertise.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:deepimagej/plugin/deepimagej.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"citations":[],"doi":"10.1101/799270","ref_count":0,"refs":[]}]}],"readme":true,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":404,"redirects":[{"status":302,"url":"https://imagej.nih.gov/ij/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"issue_tracking":{"public_tracker":true,"resolve_time":"PT1437140S"}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/deepimagej","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"readme":true,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":404,"redirects":[{"status":302,"url":"https://imagej.nih.gov/ij/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"issue_tracking":{"public_tracker":true,"resolve_time":"PT1437140S"}}}]},"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p><a href=\"https://deepimagej.github.io/\">DeepImageJ</a><span> is a user-friendly plugin that enables the use of a variety of pre-trained deep learning models in </span><a href=\"https://imagej.nih.gov/ij/\">ImageJ</a><span> and </span><a href=\"https://imagej.net/\">Fiji</a><span>. The plugin bridges the gap between deep learning and standard life-science applications. DeepImageJ runs image-to-image operations on a standard CPU-based computer and does not require any deep learning expertise. </span></p>\n\n<p>Training developper constructs and upload trained model, and made them available to users.</p>\n\n<p>Models are available in a repository <a href=\"https://deepimagej.github.io/models.html\">here</a>.</p>\n\n<p>It is macro recordable. It is advised to use DeepImageJ on a computer with GPU (CPU will likely be 20x slower)</p>","summary":"","value":"<p><a href=\"https://deepimagej.github.io/\">DeepImageJ</a><span> is a user-friendly plugin that enables the use of a variety of pre-trained deep learning models in </span><a href=\"https://imagej.nih.gov/ij/\">ImageJ</a><span> and </span><a href=\"https://imagej.net/\">Fiji</a><span>. The plugin bridges the gap between deep learning and standard life-science applications. DeepImageJ runs image-to-image operations on a standard CPU-based computer and does not require any deep learning expertise. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Training developper constructs and upload trained model, and made them available to users.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Models are available in a repository <a href=\"https://deepimagej.github.io/models.html\">here</a>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It is macro recordable. It is advised to use DeepImageJ on a computer with GPU (CPU will likely be 20x slower)</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2023-04-27T11:25:18+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2020-03-03T14:08:47+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"